# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7) Kubernetes / Oracle tooling — hand-installed in /usr/local/bin on WSL,
#    in active daily use (14 kube contexts, ~/.config/helm, ~/.config/argocd).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
brew "kubernetes-cli"     # provides `kubectl` — formula is NOT named `kubectl`
brew "helm"
brew "argocd"
cask "sqlcl"              # replaces the manual ~/opt/sqlcl install

# Go dev tools: install on demand with `go install` (dlv, gopls, goimports,
# mcp-grafana) — brew equivalents exist (delve, gopls, shfmt, golangci-lint)
# if version-managing them centrally becomes preferable.
#
# Not available in Homebrew at all — install another way:
#   pinniped (/usr/local/bin/pinniped)  -> vendor release or a custom tap
#   the npm -g packages (codex, copilot, gemini-cli, pi-coding-agent,
#     ccusage, context-mode, pi-web-access, taskplane, opencode-ai,
#     @bitwarden/cli)
#     -> npm after mise node. `npm i -g opencode-ai` (NOT brew — see §4);
#     update the same way — the built-in `opencode upgrade` self-replaces the
#     binary behind npm's back. Config: opencode/config.json -> ~/.config/opencode/
#     `npm i -g @bitwarden/cli` gives `bw` (vault CLI; the cask below is the
#     GUI). Also NOT brew: the bitwarden-cli formula depends on node and would
#     shadow mise, same trap as opencode. NOTE npm resolves to 2026.6.0, not
#     the 2026.7.0 dist-tag — 2026.7.0 pins `engines.node ~22` and mise runs
#     node 24. Do not --force past it; revisit when upstream widens engines.
#     Server URL is per-machine state (`bw config server <url>`), deliberately
#     NOT stored here — MIC runs a self-hosted instance; see the private overlay.
#     npm hardening: `npm config set strict-allow-scripts true` on every rebuild
#     (2026-08-20) — blocks dependency lifecycle hooks (Shai-Hulud-class worms);
#     verified cold npx MCP handshakes (context7, chrome-devtools) still pass.
#     If an install legitimately needs hooks: for npx/`npm exec`/`npm i -g`,
#     per-package `--allow-scripts=pkg`; project-scoped install/ci/update/
#     rebuild REJECTS that flag — allowlist via `allowScripts` in package.json
#     (`npm approve-scripts`). Never flip the global off.
#     ~/.npmrc stays machine-local, NOT symlinked —
#     npm login/registry tokens land in it, and a repo link would git-track them.
#   ae, agent, agy, claude, dev-session, graph-token, grok -> their own
#     installers (codebase-memory-mcp dropped 2026-07-29, do not reinstall)
